{"author":{"id":"f4f7e123ea38957901744390924e1710825e6d55b5113472173231f66fb2d926"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793957990,"nonce":"+ILyDMfCJxUxx4671XDg1gSx40o=","title":"CI: automate FreeDOS runtime smoke for both DOS builds","message":"Current GitHub CI cross-compiles DOS16/DOS32 and checks artifact sizes, but it does not execute either DOS binary. The v0.18.1 manual FreeDOS/QEMU validation found real regressions that successful cross-builds did not detect (near-heap exhaustion and compute-loop break handling). Add a reproducible runtime smoke job for both targets, preferably using an openly redistributable FreeDOS boot fixture and an owned disposable disk. Reuse the existing keyboard/cursor and saved-output checks where feasible; make missing prerequisites an explicit unavailable check rather than a green SKIP. Document and bound runtime/resource needs. Preserve manual graphics/audio fidelity limits.\n\nExisting local driver/evidence: /home/evaletov/.local/share/gwbasic-2026/reviews/2026-11-05-2e415fd/dos-runtime/. Repository starting points: tests/run_freedos_qemu_auto.sh, tests/run_dos_smoke.sh and .github/workflows/ci.yml. The old script requires local QEMU/images/mount support and is not immediately portable to GitHub CI. This is a follow-up after v0.18.1, not a claim that runtime CI already exists.","files":null}]}